The standalone comparison adds Gaussian acceleration noise with standard
deviation \(0.08\,\mathrm{m/s^2}\) and a constant bias of
\(0.10\,\mathrm{m/s^2}\). Each backend then receives the same causal
conditioning: a \(0.01\,\mathrm{Hz}\) DC-removal filter followed by two
\(0.8\,\mathrm{Hz}\) low-pass poles. All states reset for each replay.
The zero-crossing hysteresis is \(0.004g\); the former \(0.04g\) setting
exceeds the weak-cnoidal signal amplitude. These are standalone benchmark
settings; deployed adapters configure their own preprocessing.
The injected corruption, input records, tracker-specific random seeds,
\(0.04\)--\(2.0\,\mathrm{Hz}\) output limits, final five-second scoring
window, and \(70\%\) pairwise disagreement limit are unchanged.
